.TH ASSEMBLE 1
.SH NAME
assemble \- replay the assembly sequence and check each motion
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B assemble
[
.B \-v
]
.I assembly.txt
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Assemble
reads an assembly file
.RI ( assembly (5))
and puts its parts in, in the order of its lines: each along its
insertion path from its start to its place, with the parts that travel
with it.
A subassembly goes together first, by its own lines, in its own frame,
and then comes in as one unit along the path of its line.
A part with no path is tried at its place.
.PP
Each motion is tried in samples, against the parts in before it in its
unit.
No sample moves a part farther than the step of its path, or turns it
more than its angle: the
.BI step " dist deg"
of its file, or the same words after its
.BR path .
One bound holds besides, which the file does not set: no sample moves
any point of a part farther than half the thinnest wall of the parts
tried, the sheet of a folded part or the thinnest wall of a solid
.RI ( interfere (1)),
so no part can pass through another between two samples.
.PP
Touching is no clash, by the test of
.IR interfere (1).
A clash is said on the standard error, once for each pair of parts and
motion:
.PP
.RS
.nf
FILE:LINE: insertion path of NAME, step K at S mm: PART clashes with OTHER
.fi
.RE
.PP
at S deg for a turn, and as insertion of NAME, at its place, for a part
with no path.
With
.BI clearance " mm"
in the file, a pair that passes nearer than that on the way, short of
the place, where parts may touch, is said as
.PP
.RS
.nf
FILE:LINE: PART passes D mm from OTHER, under the clearance C
.fi
.RE
.PP
the distance within about 0.05 mm, the chord of the meshes it is
measured on; without a clearance nothing is said of distances.
.TP
.B \-v
Print a line for each motion,
.BI path " name " steps " k " samples " n" .
.SH EXAMPLES
assemble chassis.txt
.SH SEE ALSO
assembly(5), place(1), interfere(1), view(1)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Exit status 1 for a clash, 0 else.
A path whose file gives no step and whose line names none is refused,
with its line.
